<title>CHILE: Bema Gold sees Chile reserves climbing.</title>
<headline>Bema Gold sees Chile reserves climbing.</headline>
<byline>Margaret Orgill</byline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian mining company Bema Gold Corp expects its gold reserves in Chile's Maricunga belt to climb to 20 million ounces from five million ounces, once the firm finishes an ambitious exploration campaign this year.</p>
<p>&quot;We're on track to have 20 million ounces of gold reserves by the end of the year,&quot; Clive Johnson, Bema's president and CEO, told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>These include Bema's half share in the recently finished Refugio mine which sits on reserves of 7.3 million ounces of gold.</p>
